        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-30 04:05:50.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-20565 tests: use EC_* layouts in sanity-ec 27a-44a",
        "message": "LU-20565 tests: use EC_* layouts in sanity-ec 27a-44a\n\nsanity-ec subtests 27a, 30b, 31a and the degraded-read subtests\n41e-44a hard-coded an EC 4+2, 4+1 or 2+1 layout with a gate of 4 to\n8 OSTs, although the geometry did not matter to what they tested.\nMost would be skipped on the 4 OST test sessions.\n\nUse the EC_ARG, EC_DSTRIPE and EC_CSTRIPE defaults that enable_ec()\nscales to OSTCOUNT and drop the gates, so they run with 3 OSTs.\nScale sizes and offsets tied to a 4-stripe row to EC_DSTRIPE, and\nput each PFL boundary in front of an EC component on a multiple of\nthe row width, with 1M stripes in 27a.  41g keeps its 2+1 layout,\nwhich only needs the 3 OSTs that enable_ec() requires.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-ec\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-ec ostcount=4\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I8fb9da8c65de7ba367f0d70b7744d57c353ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
